{0 Workers AI}

{!Workero.Ai} runs models on
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/}Workers AI}. In both local
development and deployment, inference uses Cloudflare's remote models and
consumes account usage. Local [wrangler dev] does not simulate inference.

{1 Configure}

{@toml[
[ai]
binding = "AI"
remote = true
]}

{1 Use}

{@ocaml[
let handler req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  let ai = Ai.of_env env "AI" in
  let prompt = Option.value (URL.query (Request.url req) "q") ~default:"hi" in
  let answer =
    Ai.run ai "@cf/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct"
      (`Assoc [ ("prompt", `String prompt) ])
  in
  JSON.response answer

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

- {!Workero.Ai.of_env} opens the binding. It raises [Invalid_argument] when
  there is no such binding, or when the binding has no [run] method.
- {!Workero.Ai.run} takes a model name and the input as a [Jsonkit.t], waits for
  the model, and returns its answer as a [Jsonkit.t]. The input fields depend on
  the model. See the
  {{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/}model catalog}.
- {!Workero.Ai.run_bytes} is the same call for a model that returns an image or
  audio. It returns the raw bytes; choose a model whose output is binary.

{1 Stream an answer}

{!Workero.Ai.run_stream} sets [stream] to [true] in the input and returns the
answer as a {!Workero.Stream.t}. Text models send server-sent events. Pass the
stream to {!Workero.Response.of_stream} to forward it to the client:

{@ocaml[
let handler _req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  let ai = Ai.of_env env "AI" in
  let events =
    Ai.run_stream ai "@cf/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct"
      (`Assoc [ ("prompt", `String "Tell me a story") ])
  in
  Response.of_stream ~headers:[ ("content-type", "text/event-stream") ] events

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

{1 Route through AI Gateway}

{!Workero.Ai.run}, {!Workero.Ai.run_bytes} and {!Workero.Ai.run_stream} take
[~gateway], made with {!Workero.Ai.val-gateway}. It sets the gateway [id], caching,
logging, a timeout, {!Workero.Ai.val-retries} and log metadata.

{@ocaml[
let gateway = Workero.Ai.gateway "my-gateway" ~cache_ttl:3600 ~skip_cache:false
]}

If the runtime fails, for example on an unknown model, the call raises
{!Workero.Js_error}. [run] raises [Invalid_argument] when the model answers with
a stream; use [run_stream] for that. [run_bytes] raises it when the answer is
not binary data. Do not set [stream] in the input of [run].

{1 Verify and deploy}

With account access, run [opam exec -- wrangler dev] and request [/?q=hello].
Confirm that the response contains the model's JSON answer. Setting
[remote = false] does not provide a local model. Deploy with
[opam exec -- wrangler deploy] and repeat the request on the deployed Worker. A
plain [workerd] configuration cannot run the actual model; workero's tests use a
stub in [test/worker/services/ai.mjs] to check request and response conversion,
not model output. Wrangler supports one AI binding per Worker. See the
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/}model catalog} and
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/local-development/bindings-per-env/}local binding support}.
